<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Clearing> linkml:description "The intent is to clear the contract." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ClearingClient> linkml:description "An organization that clears trades through a clearing house, via a clearing broker (member of the clearing house) who acts as an agent on its behalf. The term 'client' refers to the organization\\'s role in the clearing process in relation to its clearing broker, and not whether it is a price maker or taker in the execution process." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ClearingCode> linkml:description "The identifier follows the symbology set by the clearing house which clears the asset." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ClearingExceptionParty> linkml:description "A party to the trade that claims a clearing exception, such as an end-user exception under Dodd-Frank Act provisions." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ClearingFirm> linkml:description "Organization that submits the trade to a clearing house on behalf of the principal. Synonyms/alternates: Futures Commission Merchant (FCM), Clearing Broker, Clearing Member Firm. Some implementations use 'Clearing Broker' as synonym." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ClearingInstruction> a linkml:ClassDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_event_common"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:attributes <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/alphaContract> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/clearerParty1> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/clearerParty2> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/clearingParty> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/isOpenOffer> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/party1> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/party2> ;
	linkml:class_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ClearingInstruction"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ClearingInstruction"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "All information required to perform the clear life cycle event; the clearing party (CCP), the two parties facing each other on the alpha contract, and optionally the parties acting as clearing members." ;
	linkml:slot_usage _:c14n1601 ;
	linkml:slots <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/clearingInstruction__alphaContract> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/clearingInstruction__clearerParty1> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/clearingInstruction__clearerParty2> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/clearingInstruction__clearingParty> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/clearingInstruction__isOpenOffer> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/clearingInstruction__party1> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/clearingInstruction__party2> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ClearingOrganization> linkml:description "The organization that acts as a central counterparty to clear a derivatives contract. This is used to represent the role of Central Counterparties (CCPs) or Derivative Clearing Organizations (DCOs). Sometimes called 'ClearingService'. Some implementations also use the term 'Clearer'." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ClearstreamBankingLuxembourg> linkml:description "ClearStream Banking Luxembourg" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Client> linkml:description "Client as defined under ESMA MIFIR. This is generally the investor or other client of an investment firm, and is synonymous with the Beneficiary in many circumstances." , "The account contains trading activity or positions that belong to a client of the firm that opened the account." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ClientDecisionMaker> linkml:description "The party or person who, having legal authority to act on behalf of a trade counterparty, made the decision to acquire or sell the financial instrument." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Close> linkml:description "The official closing time of the exchange on the valuation date." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/CloseOfBusiness> linkml:description "The valuation time should be at close of business." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Closed> linkml:description "The position has been closed, in case of a termination event." .
