<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Seller> linkml:description "A counterparty in a trade, which performs in one of the following capacities: 1) it transfers or agrees to transfer in the future an instrument or title to that instrument in exchange for payment, 2) it writes a derivatives instrument such as an option or a swap in which it provides risk protection to the buyer. This does not refer to the broker/dealer or other organization on what is typically called the 'Sell side'; for that, see the 'Executing Broker' role. Corresponds to 'Seller' as defined in certain regulations such as ESMA MiFID II/MIFIR RTS 22 field 16." , "Seller of the legal title to the financial instrument." , "Specifies that only the option seller has the right to exercise." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/SellerDecisionMaker> linkml:description "The party or person who, having legal authority to act on behalf of the trade counterparty acting as Seller as defined in this coding scheme, made the decision to sell the financial instrument. Corresponds to 'seller decision maker' as defined in ESMA\\'s MIFIR RTS 23 report. This does not refer to the decision maker for what is traditionally called the 'Sell side'; for that, see the 'Trader' person role." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/SellerHub> linkml:description "The hub code of the seller." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Senior> linkml:description "Denotes debt which ranks pari passu with all other unsecured creditors of the issuer." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/SeniorLossAbsorbingCapacity> linkml:description "Senior Loss Absorbing Capacity (RED Tier Code: SNRLAC)." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/SeniorSec> linkml:description "Senior domestic (RED Tier Code: SECDOM)." .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/SeniorUnSec> linkml:description "Senior foreign (RED Tier Code: SNRFOR)." .
