<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/fixedSettlement> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "Used for Recovery Lock, to indicate whether fixed Settlement is Applicable or Not Applicable. If Buyer fails to deliver an effective Notice of Physical Settlement on or before the Buyer NOPS Cut-off Date, and if Seller fails to deliver an effective Seller NOPS on or before the Seller NOPS Cut-off Date, then either: (a) if Fixed Settlement is specified in the related Confirmation as not applicable, then the Seller NOPS Cut-off Date shall be the Termination Date; or (b) if Fixed Settlement is specified in the related Confirmation as applicable, then: (i) if the Fixed Settlement Amount is a positive number, Seller shall, subject to Section 3.1 (except for the requirement of satisfaction of the Notice of Physical Settlement Condition to Settlement), pay the Fixed Settlement Amount to Buyer on the Fixed Settlement Payment Date; and (ii) if the Fixed Settlement Amount is a negative number, Buyer shall, subject to Section 3.1 (except for the requirement of satisfaction of the Notice of Physical Settlement Condition to Settlement), pay the absolute value of the Fixed Settlement Amount to Seller on the Fixed Settlement Payment Date." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/boolean> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/fixing> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "The default fixing details." ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/FloatingRateIndexFixingDetails> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/fixingDate> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "The date on which the fixing is scheduled to occur." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/AdjustableDate> ;
	linkml:required true .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/fixingDates> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "The fixing dates are the dates on which the index values are observed. The fixing dates are specified by reference to the reset date through business days offset and an associated set of financial business centers. Normally these offset calculation rules will be those specified in the ISDA definition for the relevant floating rate index (ISDA's Floating Rate Option). However, non-standard offset calculation rules may apply for a trade if mutually agreed by the principal parties to the transaction." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RelativeDateOffset> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/fixingOffset> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "Parameters defining the normal fixing offset (can vary by index tenor / designated maturity)." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/BusinessDayOffset> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/fixingOffsetDefinition> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "Legal text that underlies the Fixing Offset. ISDA Fixing Offset Definition. (e.g. One day that is either a Sydney Business Day or a Melbourne Business Day following the Reset Date)" ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/string> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/fixingOffsetReason> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "Fixing Offset Reason" ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/string> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/fixingPeriod> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
