<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/publiclyAvailableInformation> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "A public information source, e.g. a particular newspaper or electronic news service, that may publish relevant information used in the determination of whether or not a credit event has occurred." , "A specified condition to settlement. Publicly available information means information that reasonably confirms any of the facts relevant to determining that a credit event or potential repudiation/moratorium, as applicable, has occurred. The ISDA defined list (2003) is the market standard and is considered comprehensive, and a minimum of two differing public sources must have published the relevant information, to declare a Credit Event. ISDA 2003 Term: Notice of Publicly Available Information Applicable." ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/PubliclyAvailableInformation> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Resource> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/publiclyAvailableInformation__publicSource> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_event"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "publicSource" ;
	linkml:description "A public information source, e.g. a particular newspaper or electronic news service, that may publish relevant information used in the determination of whether or not a credit event has occurred. ISDA 2003 Term: Public Source." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/PubliclyAvailableInformation> ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/PubliclyAvailableInformation> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/string> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/publicSource"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/publiclyAvailableInformation__specifiedNumber> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_event"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "specifiedNumber" ;
	linkml:description "The minimum number of the specified public information sources that must publish information that reasonably confirms that a credit event has occurred. The market convention is two. ISDA 2003 Term: Specified Number." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/PubliclyAvailableInformation> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/PubliclyAvailableInformation> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/integer> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/specifiedNumber"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/publiclyAvailableInformation__standardPublicSources> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_event"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "standardPublicSources" ;
	linkml:description "If this element is specified and set to 'true', indicates that ISDA defined Standard Public Sources are applicable." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/PubliclyAvailableInformation> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/PubliclyAvailableInformation> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/boolean> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/standardPublicSources"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/publisher> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/common_domain_model_keys"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:definition_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/publisher"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	linkml:description "The CDM's publisher attribute; each class's slot_usage gives its meaning." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/LegalAgreementIdentification> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/LegalAgreementIdentification> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/string> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/publisher"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/purchaserSecurity> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "Defines the underlier for the Purchaser Company involved in Merger corporate action." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Security> ;
	linkml:required true .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/purchaserSecurityPrice> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "The price observation that relates to underlier for the Purchaser Company." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Price> ;
	linkml:required true .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/putCall> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "Specifies the embedded option feature of a debt security." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/PutCallEnum> ;
	linkml:value_presence "PRESENT" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/qualification> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n1262 ;
	linkml:description "The Custodian Risk or Collateral Manager Risk qualification." , "The qualification of the Pledgor Additional Rights Event election, when specified." , "The timestamp qualifier is specified through an enumeration because the experience of integrating the DTCC and CME data representations suggests that a wide set of timestamps are currently utilized among service providers, while there is not at present an objective set of criteria that could help suggest a defined set of timestamps as part of the CDM. At some future point, one possible baseline could be developed from the review of the set of timestamps specified across regulatory regimes and regulations (incl. regulations such as high frequency trading). Also, the integration with a further set of implementations and the specification of business workflows such as clearing as part of the CDM development should help confirm the implementation approach in this respect." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/EventTimestampQualificationEnum> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/string> ;
	linkml:required true .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/qualifyingParticipationSeller> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "If Direct Loan Participation is specified as a deliverable obligation characteristic, this specifies any requirements for the Qualifying Participation Seller. The requirements may be listed free-form. ISDA 2003 Term: Qualifying Participation Seller." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/string> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantity> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n2561 , _:c14n2562 , _:c14n2563 , _:c14n489 ;
	linkml:description "Represents the amount of the asset to be transferred. The cashflow amount is always a positive number, as the cashflow direction is implied by the payer/receiver attribute." , "Specifies a quantity schedule for the underlier, which applies to each individual return leg." , "Specifies a quantity schedule to be associated to an individual underlier that is a basket constituent. The multiple cardinality is aligned to the one of the PriceQuantity->quantity that this quantity is referencing." , "Specifies a quantity to be associated with an event, for example a trade amount." , "Specifies quantity amount returned if not the full amount from the TradeState, e.g. partial return" , "Specifies the quantity of shares and cash to be returned in a partial return event." , "The quantity of the security" ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/NonNegativeQuantity> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/NonNegativeQuantitySchedule> , <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Quantity> ;
	linkml:required true .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantityChange> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "Specifies instructions describing an quantity change primitive event." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityChangeInstruction> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantityChangeInstruction__change> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_event_common"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "change" ;
	linkml:description "Quantity by which the trade is being increased, decreased or replaced, and the price at which such quantity change is agreed. The quantity change should always be specified as a positive number, with the direction (increase/decrease/replacement) being specified by the direction enumeration. A fee can also be associated to the quantity change by specifying a Price component of type CashPrice, including the corresponding settlement date and direction." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityChangeInstruction> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityChangeInstruction> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/PriceQuantity> ;
	linkml:required true ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/change"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantityChangeInstruction__direction> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_event_common"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "direction" ;
	linkml:description "Direction of the quantity change specified as either an increase, decrease or replacement." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityChangeInstruction> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityChangeInstruction> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityChangeDirectionEnum> ;
	linkml:required true ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/direction"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantityChangeInstruction__lotIdentifier> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_event_common"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "lotIdentifier" ;
	linkml:description "Identifier for the new lot (in case of increase) or for the existing lot to be changed(in case of decrease or replacement). This optional attribute is mandatory in case of a decrease or replacement if the initial trade state contains multiple trade lots." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityChangeInstruction> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityChangeInstruction> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Identifier> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/lotIdentifier"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantityMultiplier> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "Quantity multiplier is specified on top of a reference quantity and is used as a multiplying factor when resolving the quantity. A quantity multiplier can only exist when the resolvable quantity specifies a reference quantity." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityMultiplier> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantityMultiplier__fxLinkedNotionalSchedule> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_product_common_settlement"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "fxLinkedNotionalSchedule" ;
	linkml:description "Multiplier specified as an FX-linked schedule, e.g. for a resetting cross-currency swap.." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityMultiplier> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityMultiplier> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/FxLinkedNotionalSchedule> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/fxLinkedNotionalSchedule"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantityMultiplier__multiplierValue> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_product_common_settlement"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "multiplierValue" ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityMultiplier> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantityMultiplier> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/decimal> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/multiplierValue"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantityReference> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n1280 ;
	linkml:description "Reference quantity when resolvable quantity is defined as relative to another (resolvable) quantity. A resolvable quantity needs to contain either an absolute quantity or a reference to another (resolvable) quantity. This requirement is captured by a choice rule on the class." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/ResolvablePriceQuantity> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantitySchedule> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n1467 ;
	linkml:description "A payout's quantity specified as a schedule, which may also contain a single value if that quantity is constant. There can only be a single quantity schedule applicable to a payout: e.g. the notional for an interest rate leg. The quantity must be specified outside of the payout in a PriceQuantity object and only referenced inside the payout using an address." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/NonNegativeQuantitySchedule> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantitySchedule__frequency> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_base_math"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "frequency" ;
	linkml:description "Defines the frequency to be used when defining a quantity. For example a quantity may be specified as a number of barrels of oil per day, which needs multiplying by the number of days in the relevant period to get the total quantity as a number of barrels." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantitySchedule> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantitySchedule> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Frequency> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/frequency"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantitySchedule__multiplier> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_base_math"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "multiplier" ;
	linkml:description "Defines an optional measure that the quantity should be multiplied by to derive a total quantity. Requires that the multiplier must be positive. This number is associated to an optional unit. For example in the case of the Coal (API2) CIF ARA (ARGUS-McCloskey) Futures Contract on the CME, where the unit would be contracts, the multiplier value would 1,000 and the mulitiplier unit would be 1,000 MT (Metric Tons)." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantitySchedule> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantitySchedule> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/NonNegativeMeasure> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/multiplier"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quantitySchedule__total> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_base_math"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "total" ;
	linkml:description "Specifies the total quantity when the quantity itself is specified with a frequency." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantitySchedule> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuantitySchedule> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Schedule> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/total"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quanto> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "If 'Quanto' is specified as the Settlement Type in the relevant Transaction Supplement, an amount, as determined by the Calculation Agent in accordance with the Section 8.2 of the Equity Definitions." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Quanto> ;
	linkml:value_presence "PRESENT" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quanto__fixingTime> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_product_template"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "fixingTime" ;
	linkml:description "The time at which the spot currency exchange rate will be observed. It is specified as a time in a business day calendar location, e.g. 11:00am London time." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Quanto> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Quanto> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/BusinessCenterTime> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/fixingTime"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quanto__fxRate> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_product_template"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "fxRate" ;
	linkml:description "Specifies a currency conversion rate." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Quanto> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Quanto> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/FxRate> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/fxRate"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quanto__fxSpotRateSource> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_product_template"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "fxSpotRateSource" ;
	linkml:description "Specifies the methodology (reference source and, optionally, fixing time) to be used for determining a currency conversion rate." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Quanto> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Quanto> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/FxSpotRateSource> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/fxSpotRateSource"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quasiGovernmentIssuerType__sovereignEntity> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_base_staticdata_asset_common"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "sovereignEntity" ;
	linkml:description "True if sovereign entity (e.g. not separate legal personality from sovereign) or false if non-sovereign entity (e.g. separate legal personality from sovereign)." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuasiGovernmentIssuerType> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuasiGovernmentIssuerType> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/boolean> ;
	linkml:required true ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/sovereignEntity"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quasiGovernmentIssuerType__sovereignRecourse> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_base_staticdata_asset_common"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "sovereignRecourse" ;
	linkml:description "Applies to non-sovereign entity (e.g. separate legal personality from sovereign). True if entity has recourse to sovereign (e.g. debt guaranteed by government). False if entity does not have recourse to sovereign." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuasiGovernmentIssuerType> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuasiGovernmentIssuerType> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/boolean> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/sovereignRecourse"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quasiGovernmentType> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "Specifies debt issues by institutions or bodies, typically constituted by statute, with a function mandated by the government and subject to government supervision inclusive of profit- and non-profit making bodies. Includes the US Agencies and GSEs and the EU concept of public sector entities. Excluding any entities which are also Regional Government." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuasiGovernmentIssuerType> ;
	linkml:value_presence "ABSENT" .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quotationAmount> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "In the determination of a cash settlement amount, if weighted average quotations are to be obtained, the quotation amount specifies an upper limit to the outstanding principal balance of the reference obligation for which the quote should be obtained. If not specified, the ISDA definitions provide for a fallback amount equal to the floating rate payer calculation amount. ISDA 2003 Term: Quotation Amount." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Money> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quotationMethod> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "The type of price quotations to be requested from dealers when determining the market value of the reference obligation for purposes of cash settlement, or which rate quote is to be observed for a fixing. For example, Bid, Offer, Mid-market or Exercising Party Pays. ISDA 2003 Term: Quotation Method. The meaning of Exercising Party Pays is defined in the 2000 ISDA Definitions, Section 17.2. Certain Definitions Relating to Cash Settlement, paragraph (j)." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuotationRateTypeEnum> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quotationStyle> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "An optional element that contains the up-front points expressed as a percentage of the notional. An initialPoints value of 5% would be represented as 0.05. The initialPoints element is an alternative to marketFixedRate in quoting the traded level of a trade. When initialPoints is used, the traded level is the sum of fixedRate and initialPoints. The initialPoints is one of the items that are factored into the initialPayment calculation and is payable by the Buyer to the Seller. Note that initialPoints and marketFixedRate may both be present in the same document when both implied values are desired." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuotationStyleEnum> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quoteBasis> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "The method by which the exchange rate is quoted." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuoteBasisEnum> ;
	linkml:required true .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quotedCurrencyPair> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n1678 , _:c14n2107 ;
	linkml:description "Defines the two currencies for an FX trade and the quotation relationship between the two currencies. This attribute was formerly part of 'fxSettlementTerms', which is now being harmonised into a common 'CashSettlementTerms' that includes a 'ValuationDate'." , "Defines the two currencies for an FX trade and the quotation relationship between the two currencies." , "Describes the composition of a rate that has been quoted or is to be quoted." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuotedCurrencyPair> ;
	linkml:required true .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quotedCurrencyPair__currency1> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_asset"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "currency1" ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n1223 ;
	linkml:description "The first currency specified when a pair of currencies is to be evaluated." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuotedCurrencyPair> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuotedCurrencyPair> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/string> ;
	linkml:required true ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/currency1"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quotedCurrencyPair__currency2> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_asset"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "currency2" ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n2223 ;
	linkml:description "The second currency specified when a pair of currencies is to be evaluated." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuotedCurrencyPair> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuotedCurrencyPair> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/string> ;
	linkml:required true ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/currency2"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quotedCurrencyPair__quoteBasis> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_asset"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "quoteBasis" ;
	linkml:description "The method by which the exchange rate is quoted." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuotedCurrencyPair> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuotedCurrencyPair> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/QuoteBasisEnum> ;
	linkml:required true ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/quoteBasis"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rate> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "The rate of exchange between the two currencies of the leg of a deal. Must be specified with a quote basis." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/decimal> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateCutOffDaysOffset> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "Specifies the number of business days before the period end date when the rate cut-off date is assumed to apply. The financial business centers associated with determining the rate cut-off date are those specified in the reset dates adjustments. The rate cut-off number of days must be a negative integer (a value of zero would imply no rate cut off applies in which case the rateCutOffDaysOffset element should not be included). The relevant rate for each reset date in the period from, and including, a rate cut-off date to, but excluding, the next applicable period end date (or, in the case of the last calculation period, the termination date) will (solely for purposes of calculating the floating amount payable on the next applicable payment date) be deemed to be the relevant rate in effect on that rate cut-off date. For example, if rate cut-off days for a daily averaging deal is -2 business days, then the refix rate applied on (period end date - 2 days) will also be applied as the reset on (period end date - 1 day), i.e. the actual number of reset dates remains the same but from the rate cut-off date until the period end date, the same refix rate is applied. Note that in the case of several calculation periods contributing to a single payment, the rate cut-off is assumed only to apply to the final calculation period contributing to that payment. The day type associated with the offset must imply a business days offset." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/Offset> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateObservation> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "The details of a particular rate observation, including the fixing date and observed rate. A list of rate observation elements may be ordered in the document by ascending adjusted fixing date. An FpML document containing an unordered list of rate observations is still regarded as a conformant document." ;
	linkml:multivalued true ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateObservation__adjustedFixingDate> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_asset"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "adjustedFixingDate" ;
	linkml:description "The adjusted fixing date, i.e. the actual date the rate is observed. The date should already be adjusted for any applicable business day convention." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/date> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/adjustedFixingDate"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateObservation__forecastRate> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_asset"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "forecastRate" ;
	linkml:description "The value representing the forecast rate used to calculate the forecast future value of the accrual period.A value of 1% should be represented as 0.01." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/decimal> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/forecastRate"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateObservation__observationWeight> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_asset"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "observationWeight" ;
	linkml:description "The number of days weighting to be associated with the rate observation, i.e. the number of days such rate is in effect. This is applicable in the case of a weighted average method of calculation where more than one reset date is established for a single calculation period." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/integer> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/observationWeight"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateObservation__observedRate> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_asset"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "observedRate" ;
	linkml:description "The actual observed rate before any required rate treatment is applied, e.g. before converting a rate quoted on a discount basis to an equivalent yield. An observed rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/decimal> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/observedRate"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateObservation__rateReference> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_asset"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "rateReference" ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n1814 ;
	linkml:description "A pointer style reference to a floating rate component defined as part of a stub calculation period amount component. It is only required when it is necessary to distinguish two rate observations for the same fixing date which could occur when linear interpolation of two different rates occurs for a stub calculation period." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:inlined true ;
	linkml:inlined_as_list true ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateReference"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateObservation__resetDate> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_asset"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "resetDate" ;
	linkml:description "The reset date." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/date> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/resetDate"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateObservation__treatedForecastRate> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_asset"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "treatedForecastRate" ;
	linkml:description "The value representing the forecast rate after applying rate treatment rules. A value of 1% should be represented as 0.01." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/decimal> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/treatedForecastRate"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateObservation__treatedRate> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	skos:inScheme "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/cdm_observable_asset"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:prefLabel "treatedRate" ;
	linkml:description "The observed rate after any required rate treatment is applied. A treated rate of 5% would be represented as 0.05." ;
	linkml:domain_of <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:owner <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/decimal> ;
	linkml:slot_uri "https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/treatedRate"^^xsd:anyURI .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateOption> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n221 ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/InterestRateIndex> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateRecordDate> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "Specifies the 'Rate Record Day' for a Fallback rate. Fallback rate fixing processes typically set the fixing rate in arrears, i.e., the Fallback Rate corresponding to a Rate Record Date is set at the end of the interest accural period. When this applies, Reset->resetDate occurs at the end of the interest period, and the Reset->rateRecordDate occurs near the start of the interest period. The Reset->rateRecordDate and Reset->observations->observationIdentifier->observationDate will differ if a Fallback rate is unavailable on the Rate Record Date, and the latest previous available rate is used as the observation." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/date> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateReference> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:annotations _:c14n190 ;
	linkml:description "A pointer style reference to a floating rate component defined as part of a stub calculation period amount component. It is only required when it is necessary to distinguish two rate observations for the same fixing date which could occur when linear interpolation of two different rates occurs for a stub calculation period." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateObservation> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateSchedule> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
	linkml:description "The fixed rate or fixed rate schedule expressed as explicit fixed rates and dates. In the case of a schedule, the step dates may be subject to adjustment in accordance with any adjustments specified in calculationPeriodDatesAdjustments." ;
	linkml:range <https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/RateSchedule> .
<https://w3id.org/lmodel/common-domain-model/rateSchedule__price> a linkml:SlotDefinition ;
